    {
      "anchor": "attaching-library-drive",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Attaching library drive"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "attaching-library-drive",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If the library drive is a CDROM media, you can attach it directly to an owned server the same way you attach a regular drive - specifying the library drive uuid."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "cloning-library-drive",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Cloning library drive"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "post--libdrives-uuid-action-?do=clone",
      "kind": "operation",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/2.0/libdrives/{uuid}/action/?do=clone"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "cloning-library-drive",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If a library drive is not a CDROM, you have to clone it in your account in order to use it. You can clone a library drive the same way you clone a regular drive."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "licensed-drive-images",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Licensed drive images"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "licensed-drive-images",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Some drives in the library may require additional subscriptions or payment to be used. This is visible from the licenses field in the drive definition. When you clone such image from drives library to your account, the licenses remain bound to the cloned drive and can’t be altered upon drive edit. See also Licenses list regarding how to list all defined licenses."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Recognizing library drives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Note that library drives can be queried through regular drives API using /drives/{uuid}/. If the drive uuid happens to be the uuid of a library drive, the drive defintion will be retrieved. In order to differentiate between owned and library drive, one can check the owner attribute, which is null for library drives."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "It is possible to get a library drive through the drives API, because there isn’t a way to know in advance whether an attached drive in a server definition is owned by the user or one from library."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Library drives are not listed in the list and detailed list for ordinary drives."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "recognizing-library-drives",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Get the drive from /drives/{uuid}/:"
    },
    {
